Significant networks constraints such as limited wireless capacity or high latency in satellite networks make centralization of data undesirable, with alternative solutions requiring coded caching and edge computing to ensure smooth service delivery in such environments. Caching involves distributing cached data to users in a coded manner, with Compress and Forward strategies being two prominent techniques. A recent approach, known as Integrated Compress and Forward, incorporates coded caching into a single framework. Distributed computing, an essential component in centralization alternatives, can also be replaced with edge computing and distributed computing solutions. A new framework combines these concepts, offering a unified approach to distributed computing and coded caching, with applications extending to resource-constrained wireless networks and MTC scenarios involving low-power, low-bandwidth connections. This framework's capabilities will be demonstrated through a case study involving a real-world MTC application. Finally, future research directions are identified to exploit the new framework's possibilities.;

